1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,848
Meet KeplerV: a desktop browser centered on goals. You describe the outcome,
then keep research, sources and follow-up steps in one workspace.

2
00:00:10,198 --> 00:00:23,654
The workspace connects a goal to tasks, helpers and saved links. Progress and
recent activity stay beside the plan, so you can return to the work instead of
rebuilding context. Type or speak a goal to get started.

3
00:00:24,004 --> 00:00:42,708
For public research, Muse can search across sites and save source-linked
findings. Each run uses your configured provider, a token ceiling, and the
goal context you explicitly approve. The NOAA, NPS and USGS links in this tour
are curated examples, not results generated live.

4
00:00:43,058 --> 00:01:01,076
The Learning Library gathers goal-related web pages, video links and PDFs.
Open supported YouTube or Vimeo resources from their cards. PDFs open in the
document view. DRM services such as Netflix hand off to the system browser;
KeplerV does not bypass playback protections.

5
00:01:01,426 --> 00:01:18,709
Helpers divide the work. Connected services use your own OAuth setup and
scoped access. A live email send needs the account, an AIP grant, and your
review of recipient, subject, message and provider. Disconnected service calls
fail closed. This demo sent no email.

6
00:01:19,059 --> 00:01:37,521
Guard explains policy decisions that block an action and keeps investigation
evidence with the runtime workspace. It can pause or contain through
configured controls. Guard covers actions routed through KeplerV policy; it is
not an all-seeing security guarantee. No incident occurred in this demo
profile.

7
00:01:37,871 --> 00:01:56,006
Phase Six adds optional public A2A agent sessions. You provide an Agent Card
or allow public web discovery. KeplerV shows the agent, destination and exact
message for your approval. Replies are untrusted input and the session
transcript is kept. This walkthrough contacted no outside agent.

8
00:01:56,356 --> 00:02:14,639
Privacy controls show which provider and endpoint would receive goal context.
Consent is per goal and provider. Token caps set usage boundaries, not dollar
estimates. Local-model data stays on this Mac only when the configured
endpoint is actually local. OAuth secrets stay in Keychain.

9
00:02:14,989 --> 00:02:28,122
Switching is supported through bookmark import and export and a portable
workspace backup. The backup gives you a manual way to move your work between
devices. Cross-device cloud profile sync is not implemented in this build.

10
00:02:28,472 --> 00:02:47,416
KeplerV brings goals, research, learning media and safety review together.
Live model, email and agent features need configuration and approval. This is
an illustrated walkthrough of the product flow: the links are curated, no live
model ran, no email was sent, and no external agent was contacted.
